    <h2>7. Website analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses <strong>first-party analytics</strong>, hosted on our own
      infrastructure (Cloudflare and Supabase), to learn in aggregate how many
      people visit and whether the site works: page views together with the
      referring site, the country, the language, the device type, and clicks
      on the download buttons.
    </p>
    <p>
      The measurement is <strong>cookieless</strong>: it stores nothing in
      your browser and uses no persistent identifier. Visitors are counted
      through a technical code derived from a key that rotates every 24 hours;
      your IP address is used only for an instant to derive that code and is
      <strong>never stored</strong>, and the code for the same visitor is
      different every day, so you cannot be followed across days or across
      websites. The data, always aggregated and anonymous, is deleted after
      90 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      As a complement, the site uses <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>
      (Cloudflare, Inc.) under the same guarantees: no cookies, no persistent
      identifiers, no fingerprinting and no profiling. That is why this site
      still asks you to accept nothing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is our legitimate interest in knowing whether the site
      works and reaches the people it is meant for (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <!-- Retención de eventos: 90 días, confirmado por Alberto el 01-sep-2026
         (jobs pg_cron purge_events + purge_client_errors, en producción). -->
    <h2>8. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account and projects</strong>: kept for as long as your
        account exists. When you ask us to delete your account, the account,
        your projects and your purchase records are deleted from our
        systems, except the data Stripe must keep under its own legal
        obligations as merchant of record.</li>
      <li><strong>Error reports</strong>: deleted automatically after 90 days
        (section 4).</li>
      <li><strong>Usage events</strong>: deleted automatically after
        90 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Local data on your computer</strong>: the "Delete all local
        data on this computer" button in Settings removes everything PreFrame
        stores on that machine. It does not delete your account or the projects
        stored in your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask us to <strong>access</strong> the data we hold
      about you, to <strong>correct</strong> it, to <strong>delete</strong> it,
      to <strong>restrict</strong> or <strong>object</strong> to its processing,
      and to receive a copy of it in a portable format. You can object to the
      processing of error reports at any time simply by turning them off in
      Settings; you can object to usage analytics by writing to us.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, including deleting your account, write
      to the address in section 10. We answer within one month. If you think
      we have not handled your data correctly, you can also complain to the
      Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener">aepd.es</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Write to us at <strong>legal@preframe-app.com</strong>.
    </p>
